msgid "Security fixes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we released Quarkus 3.27.5, our next maintenance release for the 3.27 "
"LTS stream."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This release contains bugfixes, documentation updates, and security fixes."
msgstr ""

msgid "It should be a safe upgrade for anyone already using 3.27."
msgstr ""

msgid "This release fixes the following CVEs:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus and direct dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-15075[CVE-2026-15075] - Eclipse "
"Vert.x: `DefaultRedirectHandler` cross-origin header propagation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-15076[CVE-2026-15076] - Eclipse "
"Vert.x: `WebClientSession` cross-domain cookie injection"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53712[CVE-2026-53712] - OnGres "
"SCRAM client: Authentication downgrade"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59888[CVE-2026-59888] - Jackson-"
"databind: `@JsonIgnore` bypass with `PropertyNamingStrategy` on Java Records"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59889[CVE-2026-59889] - Jackson-"
"databind: `@JsonView` bypass for `@JsonUnwrapped` properties during "
"deserialization"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-8484[CVE-2026-8484] - Jansi: Heap-"
"based buffer overflow in JNI ioctl() wrapper"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55405[CVE-2026-55405] - "
"LangChain4j: SQL injection in embedding store metadata filter"
msgstr ""

msgid "Netty"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This release upgrades Netty to 4.1.136.Final, which fixes numerous security "
"vulnerabilities including:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55833[CVE-2026-55833] - Zip bomb "
"vulnerability in `netty-codec-http`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59921[CVE-2026-59921] - Improper "
"CR/LF neutralization in `netty-codec-http` (multipart)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59919[CVE-2026-59919] - Improper "
"CR/LF neutralization in `netty-codec-haproxy`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55851[CVE-2026-55851] - Memory "
"exhaustion in `netty-codec-haproxy`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-56745[CVE-2026-56745] - Memory "
"exhaustion in `netty-codec-http`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59899[CVE-2026-59899] - Memory "
"exhaustion in `netty-codec-http`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-55831[CVE-2026-55831] - Resource "
"exhaustion/DoS in `netty-codec-http`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-56819[CVE-2026-56819] - Memory "
"leak in `netty-codec-http2`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59900[CVE-2026-59900] - Improper "
"header neutralization in `netty-codec-http2`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59898[CVE-2026-59898] - Protocol "
"version confusion in `netty-codec-http` (websocket)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-56746[CVE-2026-56746] - Improper "
"access control in `netty-codec-http` (CORS)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For the full list, see the https://netty.io/news/2026/07/09/4-1-136-Final."
"html[Netty 4.1.136.Final release announcement]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.27, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.27."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/3.27.5[the "
"full changelog of 3.27.5 on GitHub]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
